WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.565 --> 00:00:06.940
SPEAKER 1: Hi, I'm [INAUDIBLE]
Google Developer Advocate.

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:10.030
I'm joined here today by Dave
Rensin, Director of Customer

00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:12.280
Reliability Engineering.

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:16.000
Now, Dave, CREs are renowned
for being able to take care of,

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:18.760
or at least expect, pretty
much any contingency, you know.

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:20.470
But there are certain
laws of nature

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:21.640
that you can take
for granted, right?

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:22.090
DAVE RENSIN: Like?

00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:23.950
SPEAKER 1: Lightning
never strikes twice.

00:00:23.950 --> 00:00:26.512
DAVE RENSIN: As far as
lightning never striking twice,

00:00:26.512 --> 00:00:28.720
that was clearly invented
by someone who never worked

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:30.400
in a data center in Belgium.

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:33.130
We had one that actually
got hit by lightning

00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:34.770
four times within a few minutes.

00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:37.030
SPEAKER 1: So avoid
taking shelter

00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:38.980
in data centers
in Belgium, yeah?

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:40.480
DAVE RENSIN: Yeah,
or maybe God just

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:42.130
doesn't like cloud data
centers in Belgium.

00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:43.990
SPEAKER 1: I think we'll
move on from there.

00:00:43.990 --> 00:00:47.417
Tell me, Dave, where can people
find more stories like this?

00:00:47.417 --> 00:00:49.750
DAVE RENSIN: Well, if you're
going to be at Google Next,

00:00:49.750 --> 00:00:51.865
you should stop by
the 5th Nine Lounge,

00:00:51.865 --> 00:00:56.050
a dedicated space where you can
meet Google senior SREs, CREs,

00:00:56.050 --> 00:00:58.990
Customer DevOps people, and
learn about all the wacky,

00:00:58.990 --> 00:01:01.960
wild, and, well,
downright weird stuff we

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:03.370
have to deal with day to day.

00:01:03.370 --> 00:01:06.060
SPEAKER 1: We look forward
to seeing you there.

